preConditionHook:
// Block new longs for blockBars bars after a failed new extreme. Price closed
// above the highest high of the breakoutLookback bars ending one bar before
// it, and within failBars bars afterwards a BEAR trend bar closed back below
// that same level. Brooks: assume the market trades down for at least a couple
// of legs and at least 10 bars, so do not buy into it.
//
// Written POSITIVELY as 'no such failure in the window', so the rule passes
// in the ordinary case and ANDs into a pane as a filter; the per-placement
// negate toggle gives the other reading (trade the failure).
//
// The scan is fully bounded: jj is the candidate failure bar inside the block
// window, kk the breakout bar it failed, and mm the breakout level's own
// window measured ONE BAR BEFORE the breakout bar -- EL's
// Highest(high, breakoutLookback)[1] evaluated at bar kk. Deepest bar reached
// is blockBars - 1 + failBars + breakoutLookback. Extremes() is EasyLanguage
// source, so the running-extreme scan uses el_gt / el_lt.
//
// The fresh-N-bar-extreme window replaces the swing high the source states,
// the same substitution the rest of this bucket makes; that is what drops the
// rule off SwingHigh and out of research grade.
//
// Not FailedBreakoutReversal, which requires the CURRENT bar to be the one
// closing back through the level and is an entry on the reversal. This asks
// whether such a failure happened anywhere in the last blockBars bars, adds
// the bear-trend-bar requirement on the failing bar, and is a standing block
// rather than a trigger.
failedHighRecently = false;
failedLowRecently = false;
for (jj = 0; jj <= (int)blockBars - 1; ++jj) {
    for (kk = jj + 1; kk <= jj + (int)failBars; ++kk) {
        lvlHigh = high[kk + 1];
        lvlLow = low[kk + 1];
        for (mm = kk + 2; mm <= kk + (int)breakoutLookback; ++mm) {
            if (el_gt(high[mm], lvlHigh)) lvlHigh = high[mm];
            if (el_lt(low[mm], lvlLow)) lvlLow = low[mm];
        }
        if (el_gt(close[kk], lvlHigh) && el_lt(close[jj], open[jj]) && el_lt(close[jj], lvlHigh))
            failedHighRecently = true;
        if (el_lt(close[kk], lvlLow) && el_gt(close[jj], open[jj]) && el_gt(close[jj], lvlLow))
            failedLowRecently = true;
    }
}
